  "override_note": "south-america-trip.html draws two explicit google.maps.Polyline 'flight' legs with hard-coded LatLng endpoints (Quito<->Bogota, and Santa Marta<->Isla Margarita), commented '/* Flight between ... */'. The generic calcRoute()-chain parser already detects the Quito->Bogota discontinuity as a flight leg (order 31, since call 5 starts at Bogota, not the previous call's end of Quito). It cannot detect the Santa Marta->Isla Margarita closing leg on its own, because that leg is never drawn by any calcRoute() call at all -- only by the second Polyline -- so the raw chain looks like a point-to-point trip ending at Taganga (order 35), not a loop. The post text ('Your best bet with this trip is to start at Isla Margarita, Venezuela and follow the route south from there... I drew direct lines between Quito Bogota & Santa Marta Isla Margarita that may need to be taken by plane instead') and the second Polyline together confirm this is actually a closed loop: Taganga (right next to Santa Marta) -> flight -> back to Isla Margarita (order 0). We therefore force closed_loop=true and mark the final stop's leg back to order 0 as a flight. We also seed exact coordinates for the four Polyline endpoints straight from the page's hard-coded LatLng values (geocode_source=legacy-polyline), instead of Nominatim-geocoding them, since the original author already pinned them precisely.",
